      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-black text-slate-900 dark:text-white tracking-tight">
          What is Square Footage?
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          Square footage is a standard unit of measurement used to quantify the <strong>2-dimensional area of a flat space</strong> where dimensions such as length, width, or diameter are measured in feet. When you multiply two linear measurements in feet, the resulting unit is <strong>square feet (ft² or sq ft)</strong>. The word "square" in front of any unit of measure simply indicates that you are measuring a flat surface, rather than a 1-dimensional line (length) or a 3-dimensional volume (cubic feet).
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          Likewise, <strong>square yardage</strong> represents area measured in yards (often used for carpeting and turf), and <strong>square meters</strong> represents area measured in meters (standard in international architectural drawings). Whether you are installing hardwood flooring, hanging drywall, painting walls, pouring concrete slabs, or planting sod in your backyard, determining precise square footage ensures you procure accurate quantities and avoid costly project delays.
        </p>
