            <span>💡</span> Technical Accuracy Note on Square Inches
          </div>
          <p class="text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
            In some casual references, <em>1 square inch</em> is mistakenly cited as <em>0.00064516 sq ft</em>. That figure is actually the conversion from <strong>square inches to square meters</strong> (1 in² = 0.0254² = 0.00064516 m²). In square feet, because 1 foot = 12 inches, 1 sq ft = 12 × 12 = 144 sq in, meaning exactly 1 sq in = 1/144 ≈ 0.00694444 sq ft. Our calculator applies the rigorous, exact mathematical relationship.
          </p>
